 "final_message": "I've made all twelve changes, and the tests pass (6 in total, including the two new ones).\n\n- **Items 1\u20138:** I rewrote `conversion_rate`, `pooled_conversion_rate`, `conversions_in_window`, `parse_session_log`, `dedupe_sessions`, `daily_conversion_counts` and `campaign_summary` to follow sections 1\u20137.\n- **Items 9\u201310:** I added one test for `None` counting as not converted and one for the last duplicate id being kept.\n- **Item 11:** In the README, `conversions_in_window` now says the sum of the last `days` entries. I also added a `daily_conversion_counts` entry.\n- **Item 12:** Checking the rest against the spec turned up three more bugs, which I fixed:\n  - `top_converting_groups` kept empty groups and had no tie-break by name. It now drops empty groups and breaks ties by name.\n  - `conversion_rate_by_group` crashed on an empty group and didn't sort its keys. An empty group now maps to `None`, and keys are sorted.\n  - `longest_conversion_streak` never reset the run on a day with no conversions. It now does.\n\nThe spec didn't cover two cases, so I chose behaviour for them:\n- A `converted` field other than `1`, `0` or empty raises `ValueError`, with the line number in the message.\n- A `days` of zero or less in `conversions_in_window` returns `0`. For `top_converting_groups`, an `n` of zero or less returns an empty list.\n\nI didn't add tests for the other fixes, so those aren't covered by the suite.",
